WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:06.560
Locked inside a royal crypt...is the&nbsp;
founder of Boletaria. The Last Hero:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:08.173
Old King Doran. 
The Last Hero is Old King Doran.
&nbsp;

00:00:08.173 --> 00:00:08.424
King Doran is the everlasting one, founder of&nbsp;
Boletaria and protector of the Two Swords.
&nbsp;

00:00:08.424 --> 00:00:11.360
Hah hah, of course, only according to legend!
But for him to be a hero, there must have been a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:16.800
crisis all those years ago..and the most likely&nbsp;
scenario is that Wyverns were terrorizing the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:22.560
land. Doran's jewel set bronze armour, is highly&nbsp;
resistant to fire damage..as is the brushwood set,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:27.360
an "old armour owned by the Boletarian&nbsp;
Royal Family since long ago."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:31.200
The brushwood set is intentionally&nbsp;
painted the colour of brushwood,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:37.760
suggesting it might have been coloured this way to&nbsp;
disguise the wearer as kindling..when in reality,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:42.480
they were the opposite. With the dragons baited,&nbsp;
they could then be dispatched. After all..
&nbsp;

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:49.760
Foolhardiness, aptly wielded, is&nbsp;
said to be the mark of a king.
&nbsp;

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:56.720
And Doran had all the marks of a king indeed. His&nbsp;
weapon, the Northern Regalia, requires strength,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.720 --> 00:01:02.640
dexterity, comprehension, and conviction&nbsp;
to wield..and just as well - for this sword&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:08.800
was left in this world to represent a choice.
It's a weapon made up of two blades - Soulbrandt,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:14.080
a weapon for those who seek soul power at&nbsp;
the expense of others, and Demonbrandt,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:18.320
a demon-rending blade that represents the&nbsp;
clarity of man., and rejection of soul power.
&nbsp;

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:23.920
Doran speaks on the power of souls, and likely&nbsp;
understood the temptation that comes with them.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:29.200
So in the years to come, Soul Arts, and the&nbsp;
choices they presented, would remain hidden.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:33.920
It was safer for mankind to be ignorant. 
And so, after the need for his superhuman&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:38.880
strength had faded, he entombed himself with&nbsp;
the two swords. The Key would remain with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:45.280
Boletarian Royal Family..but Doran himself, a&nbsp;
veritable demi-god..would pass into legend. 
&nbsp;

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:48.880
But in the dark state of our land,&nbsp;
legends are all we can depend upon…
&nbsp;

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:55.360
No thanks to Boletaria, the world saw the rise&nbsp;
of Monumental civilisation, a magic-based society&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.360 --> 00:02:01.600
that "controlled the world" owing to their mastery&nbsp;
of the soul arts. In their insatiable pursuit of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:08.560
power, they discovered the Old One, and worshipped&nbsp;
it as an unfathomable deposit of Soul Energy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:17.760
Alas, this lust for power was exactly the warning&nbsp;
posed by Soulbrandt..and it awoke the Old One,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:22.800
marking the beginning of the First Scourge. 
Demons ravaged the world, amassing countless&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:26.960
souls, and covering the world&nbsp;
in a deep, impenetrable fog.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:31.600
By the time the Monumentals had fought off the&nbsp;
demons and led the Old One back to slumber,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:38.000
the world as they knew it was lost.
But Boletaria, had survived. 
&nbsp;

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:46.000
In order to mend the fabric of what land still&nbsp;
remained, we entrusted six leaders with six&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:48.560
precious Archstones.
...
&nbsp;

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:52.160
One to the king of a small,&nbsp;
yet industrious land...
&nbsp;

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:58.800
In the original Japanese text, rather than the&nbsp;
king being "industrious", the king is called&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:05.120
"Ambitious". This is an important distinction..for&nbsp;
an ambitious king would have envied the control&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:10.800
the Monumentals once held over the world..and&nbsp;
spied a chance to take it for himself.
&nbsp;

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:14.800
For the time of the Monumentals had passed&nbsp;
- and the Soul Arts had been banned,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:20.480
so that their mistakes could not be repeated. But&nbsp;
Boletaria didn't need soul power - they never had.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:27.200
Not since the days of Old King Doran, who had set&nbsp;
in stone a legacy that represented caution against&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:32.240
the Soul Arts. Unlike the rest of the world,&nbsp;
Boletaria had survived on their own strength,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:39.280
fostering a culture of honour and discipline,&nbsp;
and a strength in steel and stone. Now the titans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:44.240
surrounding them were wounded fledglings,&nbsp;
flailing helplessly without their magic.
&nbsp;

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:49.120
Who can blame the fox to pounce?
Over the span of twelve generations,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:56.240
the bloodline of King Allant worked to expand this&nbsp;
small nation. We see evidence of their conquest in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.240 --> 00:04:02.560
most areas of the game, after all. In Stonefang,&nbsp;
miners fuel the Boletarian war machine, extracting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:07.920
and forging ore under the watchful eye of the&nbsp;
fat officials. In Latria, the King's own son&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:13.440
has departed with some of their rarest treasures,&nbsp;
and a legendary archer from the Shrine of Storms,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:18.480
now commands her phalanx for Boletaria.
Generations of war gave rise to many famous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:24.880
heroes - Alfred, the Tower Knight..a mobile&nbsp;
fortress. Metas, the Penetrator, a walking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.880 --> 00:04:31.920
cavalry..and recently, his Majesty's Twin Fangs&nbsp;
- Biorr, master of the Greatsword..and Vallarfax,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.920 --> 00:04:36.800
who held both wit - and the blade. 
Heroes to inspire the common troops,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:46.240
who head off to war, clad in iron, and clutching&nbsp;
their blue lotus..a token from their loved ones,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:51.440
who pray they do not bleed out in battle.
But not all soldiers in Boletaria&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:55.280
drop the blue lotus..
These "dreglings" are actually called&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.280 --> 00:05:00.720
"slave soldiers" in the original Japanese. They&nbsp;
are the lowest of the low - victims of conquest,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:06.800
mercilessly sent back into war&nbsp;
by their new masters. In fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:16.080
the one dregling who speaks on the matter&nbsp;
comments slyly that the demons themselves,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:18.640
may make better masters, for at least the demons&nbsp;
don't send them into impossible battles.
&nbsp;

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:22.960
But hell, at least the demons don't&nbsp;
send us to our deaths in battle!
&nbsp;

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:30.080
But what choice do they have? Stationed on the&nbsp;
castle outskirts are the execution grounds, where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:36.640
the King's own executioner Miralda is tasked with&nbsp;
eliminating his enemies. Defy his Majesty's will,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:41.120
and Miralda will make an example of you -&nbsp;
with many a slave soldier already condemned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.120 --> 00:05:47.760
to become a raging spirit, even in death.
You wretched traitor to the king!
&nbsp;

00:05:48.720 --> 00:05:56.080
So they stitch themselves up, and strew together&nbsp;
what defenses they can scavenge - living corpses,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.080 --> 00:05:59.520
paving the way for the.."great&nbsp;
heroes" of Boletaria.
&nbsp;

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:14.800
The king, his knights and his subjects were modest&nbsp;
and plain, but also steadfast and compassionate. 
&nbsp;

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:20.800
I have spent much time in my studies in&nbsp;
the cultured countries of the south, yet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.800 --> 00:06:22.436
no country holds my heart as does Boletaria.”
History is written by the victors, after all.
&nbsp;

00:06:22.436 --> 00:06:23.200
May light shine upon our Lord&nbsp;
and our proud Boletaria!
&nbsp;

00:06:24.720 --> 00:06:28.880
By this point, magic, and the soul&nbsp;
arts, were but a distant memory. Yes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.880 --> 00:06:31.760
Boletaria had thrived without&nbsp;
their use - but their other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.760 --> 00:06:37.920
sins had become too numerous to count.
Slave soldiers, conquest, deception.. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.920 --> 00:06:43.520
is the legacy King Allant the Twelfth inherited&nbsp;
on the day of his coronation. To his credit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:43.520 --> 00:06:48.960
it is said that he cared for his subjects, and&nbsp;
fought valiantly on their behalf..but remember:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.960 --> 00:06:55.360
Boletaria is the conqueror..not the conquered..and&nbsp;
Allant was facing pressure to expand the kingdom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.360 --> 00:06:57.885
as his fathers had done before him.
honour and chivalry would have to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.885 --> 00:06:57.999
put aside - for there were still frontiers yet&nbsp;
to conquer, and he had a familial duty to see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.999 --> 00:06:58.099
it through. Twelve generations of Allant&nbsp;
kings had led to this point by any means&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.099 --> 00:07:01.440
necessary..and by all means, it would continue.
And so, for the first time in twelve generations,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:01.440 --> 00:07:05.600
he decided to take up a sword&nbsp;
from the Old King's Mausoleum.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.600 --> 00:07:12.880
But which would he choose? His hand passed over&nbsp;
Demonbrandt, to pull Soulbrandt from its grave,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.680 --> 00:07:19.280
keeping it ever by his side. There were no demons&nbsp;
where he was slaying, after all..only men.
&nbsp;

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:25.280
His path from here was to become increasingly&nbsp;
lonely: by the time he reached old age,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.280 --> 00:07:32.880
only two were left in his life: his son, Prince&nbsp;
Ariona..and Rydell, Lord of the Frontier.
&nbsp;

00:07:32.880 --> 00:07:38.720
Despite being middle-aged, Lord Rydell is referred&nbsp;
to as "Little Allant", implying that he is the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:43.840
elderly King's younger brother, or a similarly&nbsp;
close relative. He certainly takes on less&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.840 --> 00:07:49.680
responsibility than King Allant - donning dirty&nbsp;
leather instead of royal garb, and enjoying more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.680 --> 00:07:56.080
of a reputation as an adventurer, than a Lord.
For there is a legend associated with Rydell.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:56.080 --> 00:08:00.560
It is said that the weapon he wields, the&nbsp;
Phosphorescent Pole..was stolen - from a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.560 --> 00:08:08.320
witch in the sky. These words bring the Maiden in&nbsp;
Black to mind. A witch, who favours a long pole,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.320 --> 00:08:12.640
living in a sky temple that hovers&nbsp;
above a hinterland of icy mountains..
&nbsp;

00:08:13.200 --> 00:08:18.800
The exact same mountains, that Rydell was&nbsp;
stationed to look over. It's too perfect.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.800 --> 00:08:26.400
All evidence points towards the King venturing to&nbsp;
this land, and the two brothers staging a raid - a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.400 --> 00:08:32.720
heist upon the temple, to take from them as they&nbsp;
had from so many others. But what the elder Allant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.720 --> 00:08:38.800
saw there, changed everything.
The King learned about the “soul”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.800 --> 00:08:43.280
and could see the potential it carried all&nbsp;
around him. With this knowledge, he returned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.280 --> 00:08:49.680
home to share these “soul arts” with his subjects,&nbsp;
and sorcery spread like wildfire, once again.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.680 --> 00:08:55.360
Spells and magic rings exploded in popularity&nbsp;
and began leaking out across the continent.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.360 --> 00:09:01.200
Having finally embraced the power of the soul,&nbsp;
Boletaria flourished like never before, so much so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:08.800
that even poor commoners could afford luxuries&nbsp;
like jade. If Allant cared for the impiety&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.800 --> 00:09:16.480
inherent in him propagating these soul arts, their&nbsp;
utility far outweighed it. By every other metric,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.480 --> 00:09:21.040
Boletaria was undeniably better off.
Within this new era of discovery, Prince&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.040 --> 00:09:25.840
Ariona embarked upon on his own investigation,&nbsp;
this time to tour the more advanced countries&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.840 --> 00:09:31.440
to the kingdom’s south. To learn unimpeded, the&nbsp;
royal dressed as your average knight in the region&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.440 --> 00:09:37.920
by the name “Ostrava”. But to be safe, his father&nbsp;
sent one of his Twin Fangs as an escort, leaving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.920 --> 00:09:43.760
Biorr to become the best known user of his weapon&nbsp;
and armor over other Boletarian knights. With the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:43.760 --> 00:09:48.320
warrior’s companionship abroad, the prince&nbsp;
acquired all manner of strange inventions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.320 --> 00:09:54.000
both mundane and magical alike. Everything seemed&nbsp;
to be going so well..but was it, really?
&nbsp;

00:09:55.040 --> 00:09:59.760
King Allant the 12th stood in his tower,&nbsp;
finally looking back at his own shadow.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:59.760 --> 00:10:03.600
And it was ugly. An empire built&nbsp;
on the ambition of his bloodline,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:03.600 --> 00:10:06.359
rooted in generations of cruelty and bloodshed.&nbsp;
This was the rotten legacy he inherited,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:06.359 --> 00:10:09.680
and he was had done nothing to stop it.
He was now totally alone - his son was abroad,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.680 --> 00:10:13.200
his wife is never mentioned, and so must be&nbsp;
assumed to be dead or absent..and Little Rydell&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:13.200 --> 00:10:21.040
is last seen in Latria, locked up in a cell. His&nbsp;
disaffection with humanity reflected in his royal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:21.040 --> 00:10:27.280
appointments - The Kingdom's day-to-day operations&nbsp;
were being run by the Fat Officials, openly shady&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.280 --> 00:10:33.120
sycophants who were only too happy to indulge&nbsp;
their King's apathy for his kingdom..abusing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:33.120 --> 00:10:37.760
their subjects at home, and abroad.
On the day of his coronation, Allant had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:37.760 --> 00:10:44.000
chosen Soulbrandt, the bane of men. With&nbsp;
none abroad left to conquer, he turned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:44.000 --> 00:10:48.720
his attention inwards, to his own kingdom.
Allant had stolen the Soul Arts from the Nexus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:48.720 --> 00:10:54.080
so it follows that the monumentals there would&nbsp;
have warned him of the consequences. Beneath the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.080 --> 00:11:00.720
Nexus was an ancient evil, a poison God placed&nbsp;
upon the world to combat man's own evil, should&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:00.720 --> 00:11:07.280
they use the Soul Arts for their own power.
"Surely you have seen for yourself… the pain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:07.280 --> 00:11:14.840
and suffering that fills this world! But&nbsp;
fight poison with poison. God is merciful,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:18.560 --> 00:11:19.520
and so, created the Old One. 
Without even the protection of his knights, the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:19.520 --> 00:11:23.040
King departed for the Nexus,&nbsp;
and unsealed the Old One.
&nbsp;

00:11:23.040 --> 00:11:26.240
Back in the time when I&nbsp;
lived below Boletaria castle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:27.200 --> 00:11:33.040
King Allant left on some strange business,&nbsp;
then returned with horrible Demons in tow.
&nbsp;

00:11:34.320 --> 00:11:37.600
Soon, the land was ravaged by&nbsp;
Demons and soul-starved madmen.
&nbsp;

00:11:38.240 --> 00:11:42.400
He had fought like a demon for&nbsp;
the sake of this legacy - now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:42.400 --> 00:11:47.840
it was time he actually became one. 
The Old One will feed upon our souls, and put&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:47.840 --> 00:11:53.440
an end to our tragic realm of existence!"
However, fate toyed with him..for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:53.440 --> 00:12:01.120
Allant is not the demon atop Boletaria - instead,&nbsp;
he became a wretched abomination, barely able to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:01.120 --> 00:12:06.000
lift himself off the ground. This Demon Form&nbsp;
more accurately reflected his suffering..and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:07.440 --> 00:12:13.200
even if imperfect, he had still gained the&nbsp;
powers of an Archdemon, and that was enough.
&nbsp;

00:12:13.200 --> 00:12:19.600
Within the fog, reality was whatever Allant made&nbsp;
it - and so we see the demons of his imagination.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:19.600 --> 00:12:25.120
Artifacts like the Purple Flame Shield had&nbsp;
pointed back to Wyverns for generations,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:25.120 --> 00:12:31.120
so Allant let them return, as demons.&nbsp;
His new knights towered higher than ever,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:34.800 --> 00:12:39.920
and his most precious demon - a&nbsp;
doppleganger, presided over it all. 
&nbsp;

00:12:42.800 --> 00:12:49.040
Betrayed by their liege, each heroic knight&nbsp;
was killed, save for Vallarfax, who escaped&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:49.040 --> 00:12:54.880
to the fog’s edge. Despite the mortal injuries&nbsp;
he suffered, the Twin Fang still managed to tear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:54.880 --> 00:13:01.680
open a fissure in the fog and warn the outside&nbsp;
world of what transpired before he died.
&nbsp;

00:13:01.680 --> 00:13:07.360
Refusing to believe the revelations, Biorr entered&nbsp;
Vallarfax’s tear only to be defeated by the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:07.360 --> 00:13:14.160
castle’s wyverns and black phantoms, the spirits&nbsp;
of his friends enslaved by the very traitor who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:14.160 --> 00:13:19.440
corrupted them. With the warrior thrown in jail&nbsp;
under the fat officials’ care and left to rot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:19.440 --> 00:13:26.960
Prince Ariona never heard back and ultimately&nbsp;
decided to enter the fog alone years later,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:26.960 --> 00:13:33.970
where his inexperience shines through.
A dead-end? No! Help Me!
&nbsp;

00:13:33.970 --> 00:13:34.356
I'll never make it! I'll be killed!
At least Biorr survives through his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:34.356 --> 00:13:34.893
incarceration, unlike Rydell who ended up dying in&nbsp;
Latria’s prison, his resulting phantom soon after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:34.894 --> 00:13:38.320
recaptured in another cell. And while Biorr will&nbsp;
eventually come to terms with the truth about the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:38.320 --> 00:13:44.400
King he admired, Ariona can’t accept what his&nbsp;
father has become, and will take his own life&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:44.400 --> 00:13:48.560
in the face of that reality. 
I began this quest to ask my father his reasons,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:50.080 --> 00:13:55.788
to drag him back to the path of righteousness.&nbsp;
But it seems it was all in vain. *death*
&nbsp;

00:13:55.788 --> 00:13:56.682
Their King truly no longer cares for his&nbsp;
subjects. He is happy to now stand by and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:56.682 --> 00:13:57.576
watch his kingdom burn, slowly starved of&nbsp;
its souls as death and misery prevail.
&nbsp;

00:13:57.575 --> 00:13:58.480
Now the land is again beset by wyverns,&nbsp;
requiring a hero to face them once more. 
&nbsp;

00:13:58.480 --> 00:14:01.920
But in the words of Ostrava,&nbsp;
"In Boletaria’s darkest hour,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:01.920 --> 00:14:03.760
legends are all it can depend upon"
&nbsp;

00:14:04.320 --> 00:14:10.160
And in the deep fog, the line between legend&nbsp;
and reality is blurred. The hero’s spirit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:10.160 --> 00:14:15.360
can be roused from its slumber. His form can&nbsp;
be made flesh, along with his fabled weapon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:15.360 --> 00:14:20.880
and armor. And he can be bound as the eternal&nbsp;
guardian to the last sword in his crypt. 
&nbsp;

00:14:21.600 --> 00:14:27.280
Demonbrandt - the sword Allant should have chosen&nbsp;
from the very beginning. Only those equal to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:27.280 --> 00:14:31.840
crown may take it, souls that rival a demigod.
Well..are you worthy?

